SPU helpers: powers of two from their bits, no ldexp/ldexpf/exp2 calls

Applies on top of 0061. spu__xf_in, spu_fi and the RI8 scale of
spu_cflts/cfltu/csflt/cuflt computed exact powers of two through libm (an
ldexp per lane; libm was 6.9% of the image-9 threads, spu_fi 7.4%). The
same values are built from their IEEE bits. Checked against verbatim copies
of the old code by tools/spu-bisect/xf-harness/cvt_harness.c: spu__xf_in on
all 2^32 inputs, spu_fi on every exponent/step/sign, the conversions on every
i8; gcc and clang: 0 mismatches.

--- a/runtime/spu/spu_helpers.h
+++ b/runtime/spu/spu_helpers.h
@@ -176,6 +176,13 @@
 #else
 static inline u128 spu_sfx(u128 a, u128 b, u128 t) { u128 r; for(int i=0;i<4;i++) r._u32[i]=b._u32[i]+~a._u32[i]+(t._u32[i]&1u); return r; }
 #endif
+/* 2^k as a double, built from its bits: exact, and no libm call (ldexp/exp2
+ * were most of the libm time in Tokyo Jungle's SPU jobs). Every caller keeps
+ * k well inside the normal range, -1022..1023. */
+static inline double spu__pow2(int k) {
+    const uint64_t u = (uint64_t)(k + 1023) << 52;
+    double d; memcpy(&d, &u, sizeof d); return d;
+}
 /* FI decodes the base and step fields produced by the hardware estimate
  * instructions; its second operand is not an ordinary reciprocal float. */
 static inline u128 spu_fi(u128 a, u128 b) {
@@ -187,9 +194,12 @@
